# Adding a directory integration (auto-launch)

**Agent:** One PR, [PR checklist](#pr-checklist). Not a social `SocialProvider` — profile in OpenQuok, member submits on the directory site; extension autofills from API `extension_config`. Social posting: **add-social-provider-integration.mdc**. Also **backend-migrations-naming**, **backend-migrations-seed**, **source-project-neutrality**, **company-brand-icons**.

**Deep reference:** `docs/auto-launch/extension-ui-patterns.md` (steps, compare rail, `profilePath` tables, manual smoke).

## Identifier contract

| Concept | Format | Must match in |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Site slug** | kebab-case (`peerpush`, `open-launch`) | `link_directory_sites.slug`, bundled logo lists below, `web/static/icons/link-directory/{slug}.svg` |
| **Opportunity slug** | per path (`standard-launch`, `free-queue`) | `link_directory_opportunities.slug` (per `site_id`) |
| **Provider slug** | `{site}-{variant}` | `auto_launch_destinations`, `link_directory_opportunities.auto_launch_provider_slug`, `destination-configs/<site>.ts` provider rows + aggregated `directoryLaunchProviders`, content script registration, tests |

Wire: `auto_launch_enabled` + `auto_launch_provider_slug` on opportunity; `auto_launch_destinations.link_directory_opportunity_id` → opportunity. Optional `picker_group_key` / `picker_group_title` for one Add Channel card with variant picker.

### Directory site logo (web dashboard + extension side panel)

One SVG per **site slug** under `web/static/icons/link-directory/{slug}.svg`. When adding a shipped directory site, update **all three** slug lists together (same site slug in each):

| Surface | Path | Used by |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Asset | `web/static/icons/link-directory/<site-slug>.svg` | Web `/icons/link-directory/…`, extension build copies from here |
| Web | `web/src/lib/auto-launch/buildDirectoryAddChannelTiles.ts` — `BUNDLED_DIRECTORY_LOGO_SLUGS`, `DIRECTORY_SITE_BRANDED_ICONS` | My Products Add Channel tiles |
| Extension | `extension/scripts/copy-static.mjs` — `shippedLinkDirectoryLogoSlugs` | Copies SVGs into `dist/icons/link-directory/` at build |
| Extension | `extension/scripts/verify-extension-dist.mjs` — `shippedLinkDirectoryLogoSlugs` | Fails build if any listed icon is missing from `dist/` |

The extension side panel loads `chrome.runtime.getURL('icons/link-directory/{siteKey}.svg')` (`directoryChannelPicker.ts`). If the SVG is not copied into the extension package, the avatar falls back to **two-letter site initials** (e.g. TinyLaunch → `TI`), not the real logo.

After edits: `pnpm --filter @openquok/browser-extension build` and confirm `dist/icons/link-directory/{slug}.svg` exists. See also `buildDirectoryAddChannelTiles.test.ts` for web tile logo URLs.

## Files to add or modify

### Database (seeds)

| Action | Path | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Add | `backend/supabase/db/link-directory/504_<date>_seed_<site>.sql` | `link_directory_sites` + `link_directory_opportunities` (`dofollow`, cost, `auto_launch_*`) |
| Add | `backend/supabase/db/auto-launch/<507+>_<date>_seed_<site>_destination.sql` | Destination rows; `extension_config` embedded on INSERT via `pnpm sync:auto-launch-destinations` |
| Regenerate | `backend/supabase/db/auto-launch/502_*_extension_configs.sql` | Via `pnpm sync:auto-launch-configs` — do not hand-edit |
| Run | `pnpm sync:auto-launch-destinations` then `pnpm backend:db:aggregate-migrations-all` | Never edit `backend/supabase/migrations/*_core_structure.sql` |

**Tier 5xx order:** `502` extension_configs UPDATE (no-op on empty table) → `503`–`506` site `*_seed_*` files (`destinationSeeds.ts` manifest). Next site seed prefix: **507+** (do not add a second configs file).

Refs: Uneed `link-directory/502_*` + `auto-launch/503_*`; PeerPush `link-directory/504_*` + `auto-launch/504_*`; Open Launch `link-directory/505_*` + `auto-launch/505_*`; TinyLaunch catalog backfill + `auto-launch/506_*`. Storage bucket: `auto-launch/500_*_seed_auto_launch_profile_media_bucket.sql` (reuse unless new bucket).

### `extension_config` (TypeScript → SQL)

| Action | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Add or edit | `common/src/auto-launch/destination-configs/sites/<site>/config.ts` — `EXTENSION_CONFIG` fixtures, `{SITE}_DIRECTORY_LAUNCH_PROVIDERS` (`hostPatterns`, `contentScriptEntry`, `defaultStartUrl`); thin re-export shims at `destination-configs/<site>.ts` may remain for imports |
| Edit | `common/src/auto-launch/destination-configs/sites/<site>/sync.ts` — per-site `ExtensionConfigDerivation` map (`pricing-queue` or `independent`); merged in `syncMetadata.ts` as `AUTO_LAUNCH_EXTENSION_CONFIG_DERIVATIONS` |
| Edit | `common/src/auto-launch/destination-configs/index.ts` — `DIRECTORY_EXTENSION_CONFIG_FIXTURES`, `DIRECTORY_EXTENSION_CONFIG_PROVIDER_SLUGS` |
| Edit (new site module) | `common/src/auto-launch/destination-configs/directoryLaunchRegistry.ts` — spread the site’s `*_DIRECTORY_LAUNCH_PROVIDERS` into `directoryLaunchProviders` |
| Edit (pricing-first variant) | `sites/<site>/sync.ts` — `pricing-queue` + base slug; variant fixture = `{ ...base, readyUrlHint: 'pricing' }` and pricing `start_url` on the destination manifest (no SQL `jsonb_set`) |
| Edit (multi-form site e.g. Uneed) | `independent` slugs in `sites/uneed/sync.ts`; `destinationSeeds.ts` `generationMode: 'composite'` when the SQL file needs a hand-written prelude |
| Edit (official tag/category/select catalogs) | `common/src/auto-launch/destination-configs/fieldCatalogRegistry.ts` — register catalog ids + handlers; wire `tagsCatalog` / `checkboxCatalog` / `selectCatalog` on fields in the site fixture |
| Edit | `common/src/auto-launch/destination-configs/destination-configs.test.ts` — provider slug list + registry drift vs fixtures when adding variants |
| Run | `pnpm sync:auto-launch-configs` + `pnpm sync:auto-launch-destinations` then aggregate migrations |

`DirectoryLaunchProvider` types and registry helpers are re-exported from `common/src/browser-extension/pageAssist.ts` for backward compatibility — **do not** add inline provider rows there.

